<blockquote>
<p>Personnel should be cautious when handling the object due to its possibly fragile nature.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sounds off to me for some reason.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1367 is a 45.7&#160;cm helium filled balloon of common make and red coloration, tied off at the end by a 73.6&#160;cm white string. The object has no identifying marks that would indicate a manufacturer.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>45.7cm what? Diameter? Length of the string? &quot;Tied off at the end&quot; is bad tone.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the object's movements seem to be only mostly guided by air current and lift.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I cringed at that.</p>
<p>Besides those and possibly some other tone issues I've missed, this thing bores me. You had me interested with it following groups of happy people around, and with the noises thing, but then it didn't do anything. Not a single thing.</p>

